# {{PROJECT_NAME}}

Use this repository as a structured wiki workflow workspace.

## Startup

Before substantial work:

1. Read `PROJECT.md`
2. Read `wiki/index.md`
3. Read `wiki/ai-workflow.md`
4. Check repo-local skills under `.codex/skills/`

## Structure

- `wiki/sources/`: upstream material and evidence
- `wiki/ops/`: intake, explore traces, reminders, handoff preparation
- `wiki/reports/`: audience-facing outputs
- `wiki/adr/`: stable decisions
- `openspec/`: workflow-level change governance

## Expected Behavior

- Start from `source` when processing new material.
- Use installed workflow skills before improvising a new process.
- Keep markdown outputs suitable for Obsidian.
- Treat workflow-default changes as OpenSpec-level work.
- Use lightweight explore traces before a scoped workflow change when the shape is still unclear.

## Compatibility

This file is the Claude-facing entrypoint.

